":"Commander's Palace","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"mhrW9O0O5hXGXGnEYBVoag","name":"Jacques-Imo's Cafe","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"8KnMSrMuTI2AtHZ2LOI8OQ","name":"Maurepas Foods","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"Zi-F-YvyVOK0k5QD7lrLOg","name":"Muriel's Jackson Square","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"JhpRI9m71ybWHkAqRdL0Tg","name":"The Avenue Pub","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"_Bi9kN_eR75G1eqIl7S3pA","name":"The Bulldog","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"AU-B663F3MPO7W-goWwwXA","name":"B Mac's","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0},{"business_id":"pKykk7lnD6Tf9wSzJYRyJA","name":"Starbucks","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0}],"text":[{"business_id":"pSgZ6x48zgkbWucfzswkzg","review_id":"iFy76NdzUt_UJEzdhwDbxA","date":"2017-11-28T22:07:42","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9599196910858154,"text_excerpt":"Been meaning to try this place ever since it opened. My friend and I had the whole day off so we decided to window shopping on Magazine St. Upon walking in, we were friendly greeted by our host/waitress. I like spicy food so I ordered the Geki-Kara and my friend ordered the Tonkktsu. Jackie really enjoyed her ramen because she ate till her bowl was empty. That's when you know it was good. My Geki-Kara has enough heat and spices to warm you up on a cold day. The noodles tasted authentic and it was a little on the firm side. The broth was rich, but oddly on the sweet/spicy side. It was tasty though. The sweetness I tasted in the broth might've came from the pork. The soft-boiled egg was on ..."},{"business_id":"pSgZ6x48zgkbWucfzswkzg","review_id":"0GEc9qpthBcVm_UwWCH1QA","date":"2021-10-21T16:25:45","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9531596899032593,"text_excerpt":"First time having ramen at this spot and it was satisfying. The restaurant is fairly small but they get you in and out fairly quickly. We ordered the tonkatsu broth and added seaweed. The soup was very flavorful and satisfying. We also had the pork buns, which were very soft and pillowy and the pork was succulent and flavorful. There aren't many ooohs and ahhhs here. However, you will get a nice bowl of ramen if that's what you're craving. Parking wasn't bad for a Saturday considering it's located on Magazine."},{"business_id":"pSgZ6x48zgkbWucfzswkzg","review_id":"KEWVZA2TW8x_RnG6CGcEng","date":"2017-09-22T15:05:24","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9491009712219238,"text_excerpt":"When I heard that a new little ramen shop was coming to Magazine St., I was excited to try it. After an AMAZING experience at Kin, my expectations were sky high. They don't open until 4, so I stuck it out for a late lunch/early dinner and walked in as soon as they unlocked the doors. The restaurant itself is SMALL and the menu is limited, but that just made it easier for me to decide exactly what I wanted. We started with the pork buns which were amazing. The pork was falling out of them and they were so good. You have two choices when it comes to the ramen: Tonkotsu, which is a creamy pork broth and Geki-Kara, which is their \"too-spicy\" pork broth. Normally I would have gone with the spi..."}],"visual":[{"business_id":"pSgZ6x48zgkbWucfzswkzg","photo_id":"JBjy3OoLlsMO1WiIau6DRg","label":"inside","image_url":"/photos/JBjy3OoLlsMO1WiIau6DRg.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.858169674873352},{"business_id":"pSgZ6x48zgkbWucfzswkzg","photo_id":"3I6W1rn9jnWiuAntP59kJA","label":"outside","image_url":"/photos/3I6W1rn9jnWiuAntP59kJA.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.8338524103164673},{"business_id":"pSgZ6x48zgkbWucfzswkzg","photo_id":"nSY2lL8l0AIT7P-kjgx8Cw","label":"drink","image_url":"/photos/nSY2lL8l0AIT7P-kjgx8Cw.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.8333516716957092},{"business_id":"pSg